1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,898
An office calendar shows who is in an office, and which desks are

2
00:00:04,898 --> 00:00:07,479
booked, up to the number of desks it has.

3
00:00:07,479 --> 00:00:11,102
This video shows how to set one up, how people mark the days

4
00:00:11,102 --> 00:00:15,055
they are in, book a desk and register a visitor, what happens when

5
00:00:15,055 --> 00:00:18,020
the office is full, and how to close the office.

6
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:26,092
When people work in the office on some days and from home on

7
00:00:26,092 --> 00:00:30,300
others, nobody knows who will be in, or whether there will be a desk free.

8
00:00:31,050 --> 00:00:34,727
An office calendar answers both questions on one page.

9
00:00:34,727 --> 00:00:38,465
People mark the days they are in, book a desk for a few

10
00:00:38,465 --> 00:00:41,590
hours, and register the visitors they expect.

11
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,453
The calendar has a desk count.

12
00:00:44,453 --> 00:00:48,444
Once that many people are in the office, or have booked a desk

13
00:00:48,444 --> 00:00:53,550
at the same time, the next booking is refused, so the office is never overbooked.

14
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,435
There are four kinds of events:

15
00:00:56,435 --> 00:00:59,783
In office, Desk booking, Visitor, and Office closed.

16
00:00:59,783 --> 00:01:03,880
Each one behaves a little differently, and you will see all four.

17
00:01:08,062 --> 00:01:11,849
Office calendars come with the Office Calendars feature.

18
00:01:11,849 --> 00:01:16,063
Open Calendars, then Manage Calendars, and choose Add calendar.

19
00:01:16,063 --> 00:01:18,812
Office is one of the types in the list.

20
00:01:19,263 --> 00:01:21,361
Here is the Lisbon office.

21
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:22,540
Choose Edit.

22
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:27,980
Besides the name, color, time zone and visibility that every calendar has, an

23
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:32,633
office has an Address, and a Contact, such as the office manager.

24
00:01:33,084 --> 00:01:39,068
Under Overlaps, the office limits overlapping events, and Events that may overlap holds

25
00:01:39,068 --> 00:01:40,741
the number of desks.

26
00:01:40,741 --> 00:01:43,186
A new office starts with twenty.

27
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:44,794
This one has three.

28
00:01:45,284 --> 00:01:48,919
Visibility is Public, so everyone can see who is in.

29
00:01:48,919 --> 00:01:52,242
Shared would show only when the office is busy.

30
00:01:52,242 --> 00:01:54,624
Choose Save to keep the changes.

31
00:01:58,825 --> 00:02:03,982
Open Calendars, then Calendar, and go to the week of the second of November.

32
00:02:03,982 --> 00:02:07,693
Jamie Chen and Sam Patel are in the office on Monday.

33
00:02:07,693 --> 00:02:12,725
An In office event lasts the whole day, and it names the person who is in.

34
00:02:13,177 --> 00:02:17,927
Choose New event, and pick the Lisbon office and the Desk booking kind.

35
00:02:18,377 --> 00:02:23,589
A desk booking lasts four hours by default, and it also names a person.

36
00:02:23,589 --> 00:02:27,717
Give it a title, set the times, and invite Riley Ortiz.

37
00:02:28,168 --> 00:02:29,389
Choose Save.

38
00:02:29,389 --> 00:02:34,748
Riley is the third person in on Monday, so all three desks are now taken.

39
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:38,456
Now register a visitor for the same morning.

40
00:02:38,456 --> 00:02:42,167
A visitor needs no person, only a title and a time.

41
00:02:42,167 --> 00:02:46,790
Choose New event, pick the Visitor kind, and fill in the details.

42
00:02:47,242 --> 00:02:51,611
When you choose Save, the office is full, so the event is refused.

43
00:02:51,611 --> 00:02:55,859
The message says the Lisbon office is already full at that time.

44
00:02:55,859 --> 00:02:59,622
Pick another time, or ask someone to move their booking.

45
00:03:03,922 --> 00:03:06,333
An Office closed event is different.

46
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:10,123
It shows on the calendar, but it leaves the time free, so it

47
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:11,673
never uses up a desk.

48
00:03:11,673 --> 00:03:16,382
Here is the office closed on the twenty-fourth and twenty-fifth of December.

49
00:03:16,856 --> 00:03:18,838
Click it to see the details.

50
00:03:18,838 --> 00:03:23,035
When the office shuts for a holiday, add one all-day event for the

51
00:03:23,035 --> 00:03:25,716
days it is closed, and everyone sees it.

52
00:03:29,916 --> 00:03:32,673
The desk count counts busy events.

53
00:03:32,673 --> 00:03:36,670
In office, Desk booking and Visitor all take a desk.

54
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:40,736
An event marked as Free, and Office closed, never do.

55
00:03:41,486 --> 00:03:45,575
New events use the office's own time zone, so a desk booked in

56
00:03:45,575 --> 00:03:47,380
Lisbon is a Lisbon time.

57
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:50,146
Everyone sees it in their own time zone.

58
00:03:50,896 --> 00:03:55,026
Who can see the office is up to its visibility and its sharing.

59
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:58,796
A disabled office keeps its events but takes no new ones.

60
00:04:00,796 --> 00:04:04,914
An office calendar keeps who is in, and which desks are booked, on

61
00:04:04,914 --> 00:04:08,289
one page, and refuses the booking that would not fit.

62
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:09,776
Thanks for watching.

